WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.730
In a group class, a live board now ranks every rider by output, sent by the service

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.899
once a second.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.242
It reads Output with your place, lists every rider by kilojoules, highest first, and

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:16.655
marks your own row.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.323
Each second the ride sends your output and power to the hub, and never more than

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:28.391
twice a second.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.612
At the start, bots fill the empty seats to ten, each riding a steady pace with a

00:00:40.612 --> 00:00:41.864
swing of its own.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.224
Pull ahead, and the next standings slide you up the board.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.408
On a laptop the board is a column beside the video; on a phone it sits underneath.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.947
What the tests prove: ranked by output, bots up to ten, reports at most twice a

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:18.906
second, and your row marked.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
